      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For more tips and advice on the nutrients you need to fuel you and your growing baby, the What to Expect app has you covered.",
        "text_sha256": "3b8ff02a441e0d71e02b371ba1e28096de16b1c3c7c49afa582fd72362b2578e",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "3. Iron-rich foods",
        "text_sha256": "caa0c3af472726286b5b6e68b7731f830a7e14e0a11c06de8911a624e94f0a95",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fatigue, especially if it's really keeping you down, could be related to iron-deficiency anemia , especially as pregnancy progresses and the demands of blood making start to take their toll.",
        "text_sha256": "cb501c3e5b406e0a98fbb30b2c5aea449e4cb8aad606c8b7bd5a85eda3ba592e",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Making sure you get some iron-rich foods daily (as well as taking your prenatal vitamin ) will keep your irons stores elevated and help pump up your energy level. You can find iron from these healthy sources:",
        "text_sha256": "d6b18d96116695a3ba33d843c269891dd618486e780e2986af7e35d40798fe40",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000049",
        "block_index": 49,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Iron-fortified cereals",
        "text_sha256": "1e7268c8b9ffac60290324d7550d51a2b028aa51287b31be2dd3bc6e869222dc",
        "word_count": 2
      },
